messages:
maria: Heads-up — a customer hit a failure on Cloudflare Workers after upgrading to SDK v0.9.0. 415 Unsupported Media Type when we retry auth requests. Anyone seen this?

sahil: I ran into something similar in e2e. Workers handles Request/Headers differently than Node. Our retry path clones Requests and ends up sending duplicate Authorization headers.

ben: Minimal repro I made:
```js
addEventListener('fetch', e => {
  const req = e.request;
  const r1 = new Request(req);
  r1.headers.append('authorization', req.headers.get('authorization'));
  // fetch(r1) -> upstream 415 for some origins
});
```

maria: The customer has NGINX + auth proxy that rejects duplicate auth. Node normalized it so it passed.

karen: CF's Headers model can make append() create multi-value header entries. Some CDNs treat multi-value Authorization as malformed.

maria: Our retry wrapper currently sets Authorization twice: once by cloning the Request (which already has it) and again via fetch init.headers. That double-set triggers the problem.

sahil: Quick fix: when retrying, construct a fresh Request with a single headers object derived from existing values, using headers.set instead of append. Example:
```js
const auth = req.headers.get('authorization');
const headers = new Headers();
if (auth) headers.set('authorization', auth);
const retryReq = new Request(req.url, {
  method: req.method,
  headers,
  body: await req.clone().arrayBuffer(),
});
```
This yields a single-value header on Workers.

ben: Also a typings issue showed up: our ESM build accidentally imports Node types (import type { Readable } from 'stream'), which forces TypeScript to pull node definitions for consumers on Workers. For edge builds we should expose web types (ReadableStream) only.

maria: We should add an explicit edge export in package.json (exports.browser or exports['.edge']) and a tsconfig.edge that uses libs ["webworker","es2021"]. That prevents node type bleed.

karen: And add a runtime feature-detect switch: prefer globalThis.fetch + ReadableStream paths for edge, fallback to node-specific code elsewhere. Feature-detect rather than package assumption.

maria: Can someone add a tiny sample under samples/edge-auth-dup that reproduces this in Miniflare CI? Keep it minimal and exercise the retry path so we can add it to regression tests.

sahil: I'll take it. I'll open a PR with two commits: (1) runtime-safe retry implementation (no append), (2) edge tsconfig + new export entry. Will include unit tests + a Miniflare integration test.

ben: Changelog: "fix(workers): avoid duplicating Authorization on retries" and mention typings fix separately.

maria: Also put a note in the migration guide: edge users may need to update custom middleware that relied on Node header normalization.

ci-bot: Created ticket RN-4321: "CF Workers: prevent duplicate Authorization on SDK retry; add edge export + typing fix" https://git.internal/redwood/rn/4321

maria: Thanks — assigning to @sahil. Please ping once the sample is live. :thumbsup:

sahil: Will do, aiming for a PR today.

karen: Small follow-up: add a lint rule to forbid headers.append('authorization', ...) in retry code paths to prevent regressions.

maria: Great idea. Adding that to the PR checklist.
